      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Forth Moving Lisp Moving Forth",
      "url": "https://letoverlambda.com/textmode.cl/guest/chap8.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/exipox",
      "score": 6,
      "comments": 0,
      "author": "LenFalken",
      "published": "2026-07-26T17:39:27Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Metacompilation techniques enable mutual bootstrapping, using a minimal Forth core to host Lisp runtimes capable of compiling target Forth systems.",
        "Unifies stack-based and S-expression paradigms, combining Forth's low-overhead execution model with Lisp's dynamic macro expansion and meta-programming capabilities.",
        "Offers lightweight, interactive REPL environments suitable for bare-metal embedded systems without requiring heavy runtime dependencies or complex OS toolchains."
      ]
    },
